]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Reset</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_EnvironmentControl</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_EnvironmentControl
  ---------------------
  Implements: I_Zone
  Responsibility: Zone C — Temperature and humidity control.

  Uses a DEADBAND control strategy:
  - Normal band: setpoint ± tolerance (cooling/heating ON/OFF)
  - Alarm band:  setpoint ± (tolerance × alarm multiplier) → alarm fires

  Example with defaults (setpoint=15, tolerance=2, multiplier=2):
    Temperature 11–13°C → Heating ON, no alarm
    Temperature 13–17°C → Both OFF (OK zone)
    Temperature 17–19°C → Cooling ON, no alarm
    Temperature <11°C or >19°C → Alarm fires
]]></Comment><BitSize>960</BitSize><Implements>I_Zone</Implements><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fActualTemp_C</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fActualHumid_Pct</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCoolingON</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHeatingON</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>232</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHumidityAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>248</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fAlarmBand</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>928</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Reset</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__setIsHealthy</Name><Parameter><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsHealthy</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getStatusMessage</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsEnabled</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setIsEnabled</Name><Parameter><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setStatusMessage</Name><Parameter><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ExpiryMonitor</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_ExpiryMonitor
  ----------------
  Responsibility: Continuous batch expiry surveillance.
  
  Runs EVERY scan cycle (no edge detection needed here).
  Checks all 20 batch records and updates their eStatus.
  
  Status progression:
    NORMAL → EXPIRING (within 30 days) → EXPIRED
  
  Once EXPIRED, the batch is NOT quarantined here.
  FB_QuarantineHandler is responsible for that action.
  This FB only DETECTS — it does not ACT on the storage.
]]></Comment><BitSize>320</BitSize><SubItem><Name>dtNow</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nWarningDays</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Days before expiry to issue warning]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><Value>30</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nExpiredCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ How many batches are currently expired]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nExpiringCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ How many are within warning period]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nNormalCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ How many are healthy]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dwNow</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dwExpiry</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nDaysRemaining</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nSecondsPerDay</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><Value>86400</Value></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_QuarantineHandler</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_QuarantineHandler
  --------------------
  Implements: I_Zone
  Responsibility: Zone D — Automatic isolation of unsafe batches.

  Runs EVERY scan cycle.
  Scans all batch records for EXPIRED or RECALLED status.
  For each found:
  1. Changes status to QUARANTINED
  2. Changes zone to ZONE_QUARANTINE
  3. Frees the rack slot (so healthy batches can use it)
  4. Sets quarantine alarm

  NOTE: Once quarantined, a batch can only be removed by
  a maintenance operator — not by the automatic system.
]]></Comment><BitSize>1088</BitSize><Implements>I_Zone</Implements><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtNow</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nQuarantineCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Total batches currently in Zone D]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bQuarantineAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE if any batch in quarantine]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sLastQuarantined</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ID of most recently quarantined batch]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>216</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1040</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bNewQuarantine</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1056</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Reset</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__setIsHealthy</Name><Parameter><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsHealthy</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getStatusMessage</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsEnabled</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setIsEnabled</Name><Parameter><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setStatusMessage</Name><Parameter><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_MedicineStatus</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_MedicineStatus
  ----------------
  Describes the current health/safety condition of a medicine batch.
  Every batch in the system carries exactly one of these states at all times.
  The lifecycle is: NORMAL → EXPIRING → EXPIRED → QUARANTINED
  A recalled batch jumps directly to RECALLED → QUARANTINED.
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_EMPTY</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Record slot unused — no batch here]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_NORMAL</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch is healthy, within expiry]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_EXPIRING</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Expiry within 30 days — dispatch soon]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_EXPIRED</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Past expiry — must be quarantined]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_QUARANTINED</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Locked in Zone D — cannot be used]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_RECALLED</Text><Enum>5</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Manufacturer recall — must be quarantined]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEDICINE_DAMAGED</Text><Enum>6</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Physical damage detected (future use)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_ZoneID</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_ZoneID
  --------
  Identifies which physical zone of the warehouse a batch is located in.
  Every batch record always knows its current location.
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>ZONE_NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Not in any zone (dispatched or not yet placed)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ZONE_RECEIVING</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Zone A — at the entry gate conveyor]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ZONE_STORAGE</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Zone B — on a rack slot]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ZONE_ENV_CONTROL</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Zone C — in controlled environment section]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ZONE_QUARANTINE</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Zone D — in isolation area]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_MedicineBatch</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_MedicineBatch
  ----------------
  The complete identity record ("passport") of one medicine batch.
  This is the most important data structure in the entire system.
  20 of these records live in GVL_MedicineDB.astBatches[1..20].
  One record = one physical box/container of medicine.
]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><SubItem><Name>sBatchID</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Unique batch code (e.g. 'BATCH_2026_001')]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sMedicineName</Name><Type>STRING(30)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Medicine description (e.g. 'Paracetamol 500mg')]]></Comment><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>168</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sManufacturer</Name><Type>STRING(30)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Manufacturer name]]></Comment><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fWeight_kg</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch weight in kilograms]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fTempRequired_C</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Required storage temperature in °C]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>704</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtEntryTime</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When batch entered the warehouse]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>736</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtExpiryDate</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When batch expires]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eStatus</Name><Type>E_MedicineStatus</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current health status]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eCurrentZone</Name><Type>E_ZoneID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current physical location]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>816</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nRackSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which slot (1–20), 0 = not in rack]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bIsOccupied</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = this array slot is in use]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>848</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nRecordIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Index in astBatches array (1–20)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>864</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ReceivingZone</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_ReceivingZone
  ----------------
  Implements: I_Zone
  Responsibility: Zone A — Validates and registers incoming batches.
  
  WHAT IT DOES:
  When a batch arrives (bBatchArrived rising edge):
  1. Checks weight > minimum
  2. Checks BatchID is not empty
  3. Checks expiry date is in the future
  If ALL checks pass → creates complete ST_MedicineBatch record
  If ANY check fails → sets bBatchRejected with a reason message
  
  RISING EDGE DETECTION is critical: bBatchArrived may stay TRUE
  for many scan cycles. We only want to process it ONCE.
]]></Comment><BitSize>3200</BitSize><Implements>I_Zone</Implements><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ From GVL_SystemState.bMasterEnable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSafeToOperate</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ From FB_SafetyInterlock]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>136</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBatchArrived</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Proximity sensor (simulated)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sBatchID</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Barcode scan result]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>152</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sMedicineName</Name><Type>STRING(30)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Medicine label]]></Comment><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sManufacturer</Name><Type>STRING(30)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Manufacturer label]]></Comment><BitSize>248</BitSize><BitOffs>568</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fWeight_kg</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Load cell reading]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fTempRequired_C</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Required storage temperature]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>864</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtExpiryDate</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ From medicine label]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>896</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtNow</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current system time]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>928</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBatchAccepted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE for one cycle when batch passes]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>960</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBatchRejected</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE for one cycle when batch fails]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>968</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stNewBatch</Name><Type>ST_MedicineBatch</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Complete batch record if accepted]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>992</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current status for HMI display]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1888</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastBatchArrived</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Edge detection]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2536</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRisingEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sRejectionReason</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Internal]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>2552</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Reset</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__setIsHealthy</Name><Parameter><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsHealthy</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getStatusMessage</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsEnabled</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setIsEnabled</Name><Parameter><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setStatusMessage</Name><Parameter><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_RetrievalResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_RetrievalResult
  -----------------
  The outcome of a retrieval operation.
  FB_StorageManager sets this after every retrieval attempt.
  HMI reads this to tell the operator what happened.
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>RETRIEVAL_NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ No retrieval has been attempted yet]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRIEVAL_SUCCESS</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch dispatched successfully]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRIEVAL_NOT_FOUND</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Requested batch ID does not exist]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRIEVAL_REARRANGING</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ASRS crane is currently in motion]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRIEVAL_FAULT</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Mechanical or system error occurred]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_StorageManager</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_StorageManager
  -----------------
  Implements: I_Zone
  Responsibility: Zone B — Manages rack slots and FIFO retrieval logic.

  WHAT IT DOES:
  STORE:
  1. Receives accepted batch from FB_ReceivingZone
  2. Finds first available free slot in astRackSlots[1..20]
  3. Sends command to FB_ASRSCoordinator with slot number
  4. WAITS for ASRS to confirm physical placement
  5. Only then marks slot as occupied in database

  RETRIEVE:
  1. If sBatchIDToGet is empty → FIFO mode: finds batch with oldest dtEntryTime
  2. If sBatchIDToGet has a value → specific batch mode: finds that exact batch
  3. Sends slot number to FB_ASRSCoordinator
  4. WAITS for ASRS to confirm retrieval complete
  5. Clears the slot in database
]]></Comment><BitSize>3968</BitSize><Implements>I_Zone</Implements><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSafeToOperate</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>136</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreRequest</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge: new batch to store]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stBatchToStore</Name><Type>ST_MedicineBatch</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch data from FB_ReceivingZone]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrieveRequest</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge: retrieve a batch]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1056</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sBatchIDToGet</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specific ID or '' for FIFO]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>1064</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtNow</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bASRS_StoreDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ASRS confirmed deposit complete]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1280</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bASRS_RetrieveDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ASRS confirmed retrieval complete]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1288</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Store</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: start storage sequence]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1296</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Retrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: start retrieval sequence]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1304</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nCmd_TargetSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which slot ASRS should use]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1312</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stCmd_BatchData</Name><Type>ST_MedicineBatch</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch data for ASRS reference]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>1344</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreSuccess</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: storage completed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when all 20 slots occupied]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2248</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eRetrievalResult</Name><Type>E_RetrievalResult</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2256</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stRetrievedBatch</Name><Type>ST_MedicineBatch</Type><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>2272</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nFreeSlots</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Counts]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3168</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nOccupiedSlots</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3184</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>3200</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastStore</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Edge detection]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3848</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastRetrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3856</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3864</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrieveEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3872</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaitingForASRS</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE while ASRS is doing work]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3880</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eCurrentOperation</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 0=idle, 1=storing, 2=retrieving]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3888</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Loop variable]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3904</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nFoundSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nOldestIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>3936</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Reset</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__setIsHealthy</Name><Parameter><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsHealthy</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getStatusMessage</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getIsEnabled</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setIsEnabled</Name><Parameter><Name>IsEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__setStatusMessage</Name><Parameter><Name>StatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_ASRSState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_ASRSState
  -----------
  The current state of the ASRS crane.
  Used by FB_ASRSCrane state machine.
  Crane follows this sequence for storage:
    IDLE → MOVING_TO_SLOT → DEPOSITING → MOVING_TO_CONV → HANDING_OVER → IDLE
  For retrieval:
    IDLE → MOVING_TO_SLOT → RETRIEVING → MOVING_TO_CONV → HANDING_OVER → IDLE
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_IDLE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane parked at home position (0,0)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_MOVING_TO_SLOT</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane traveling to target rack slot]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_DEPOSITING</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane lowering batch into slot (store)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_RETRIEVING</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane gripping batch from slot (retrieve)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_MOVING_TO_CONV</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane returning to conveyor handoff point]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_HANDING_OVER</Text><Enum>5</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Crane placing batch on output conveyor]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASRS_FAULT</Text><Enum>6</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Hardware error — manual intervention needed]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_ConveyorState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_ConveyorState
  ---------------
  The current mechanical state of one conveyor belt.
  Used by FB_ConveyorControl state machine.
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_IDLE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Belt stopped, waiting for command]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_MOVING</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Belt running normally]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_BLOCKED</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Physical obstruction detected]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_FAULT</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Motor/drive hardware failure]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_ConveyorDirection</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_ConveyorDirection
  -------------------
  Which direction the conveyor belt is running.
  FORWARD = toward ASRS entry point (for storing)
  REVERSE = toward dispatch exit (for retrieving)
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_DIR_NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Belt is stopped]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_DIR_FORWARD</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Moving toward ASRS crane entry]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONV_DIR_REVERSE</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Moving toward dispatch exit]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_ConveyorStatus</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_ConveyorStatus
  -----------------
  Complete state description of one conveyor belt.
  Two instances in GVL_MedicineDB:
    stInputConveyor  — belt from Zone A gate to ASRS entry
    stOutputConveyor — belt from ASRS exit to dispatch point
]]></Comment><BitSize>672</BitSize><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_ConveyorState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current mechanical state]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eDirection</Name><Type>E_ConveyorDirection</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current running direction]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBatchOnBelt</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Is a batch currently riding this belt?]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sBatchIDOnBelt</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which batch (empty if belt is clear)]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAtASRSEntry</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch has reached ASRS entry sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAtDispatch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch has reached dispatch exit sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>216</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fBeltSpeed_ms</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current belt speed (m/s)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = fault condition]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sFaultMessage</Name><Type>STRING(50)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Fault description]]></Comment><BitSize>408</BitSize><BitOffs>264</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Name><BitSize>256</BitSize><SubItem><Name>IN</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ starts timer with rising edge, resets timer with falling edge ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PT</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ time to pass, before Q is set ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Q</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ gets TRUE, delay time (PT) after a rising edge at IN ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ET</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ elapsed time ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>M</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StartTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ConveyorControl</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_ConveyorControl
  ------------------
  Manages ONE physical conveyor belt as a state machine.
  FB_ASRSCoordinator creates TWO instances:
    fbInputConv  — carries batches from Zone A gate TO ASRS crane entry
    fbOutputConv — carries batches FROM ASRS crane exit TO dispatch area

  STATE MACHINE:
    CONV_IDLE ──(start fwd)──► CONV_MOVING ──(at ASRS entry)──► CONV_IDLE (bAtASRSEntry=TRUE)
    CONV_IDLE ──(start rev)──► CONV_MOVING ──(at dispatch)────► CONV_IDLE (bAtDispatch=TRUE)
    CONV_MOVING ──(blocked)──► CONV_BLOCKED
    CONV_MOVING ──(timeout)──► CONV_FAULT
]]></Comment><BitSize>1472</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_StartForward</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: run toward ASRS entry]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_StartReverse</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: run toward dispatch exit]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Stop</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: stop belt immediately]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_BatchAtEntry</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Proximity sensor at ASRS entry]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_BatchAtDispatch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Proximity sensor at dispatch exit]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_Blocked</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Obstruction sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fSim_BeltSpeed_ms</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Speed setpoint]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stStatus</Name><Type>ST_ConveyorStatus</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Complete belt status]]></Comment><BitSize>672</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bMotorON</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Motor contactor output]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>840</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonTravelTimer</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max time for batch to reach sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>896</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonBlockTimeout</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Watchdog for blockage duration]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastFwd</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Edge detection]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1408</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastRev</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFwdEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1424</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRevEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1432</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_ASRSPosition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_ASRSPosition
  ---------------
  Describes a physical position of the ASRS crane.
  Used both for current position and target position.
  Two instances in GVL_MedicineDB:
    stASRS_CurrentPos — where the crane IS right now
    stASRS_TargetPos  — where the crane NEEDS to go
]]></Comment><BitSize>160</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nColumn</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Target column (1–4)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nRow</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Target row (1–5)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nSlotNumber</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Target slot (1–20), 0 = home position]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fX_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Horizontal distance from home]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fY_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Vertical height from ground]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAtTarget</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = crane has reached this position]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ASRSCrane</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_ASRSCrane
  ------------
  Controls the ASRS robotic crane — the heart of Zone B.

  PHYSICAL MODEL:
  The crane runs on two axes:
    X axis (horizontal) — moves between 4 columns
    Y axis (vertical)   — moves between 5 rows
  
  Slot-to-physical position formula:
    Column = ((SlotNumber - 1) MOD 4) + 1
    Row    = ((SlotNumber - 1) / 4) + 1
    X_mm   = C_FIRST_COL_X_MM + (Column-1) × C_COL_SPACING_MM
    Y_mm   = C_FIRST_ROW_Y_MM + (Row-1)    × C_ROW_SPACING_MM

  STATE MACHINE:
  For STORE:
    IDLE → MOVING_TO_SLOT → DEPOSITING → MOVING_TO_CONV → HANDING_OVER → IDLE
  For RETRIEVE:
    IDLE → MOVING_TO_SLOT → RETRIEVING → MOVING_TO_CONV → HANDING_OVER → IDLE
]]></Comment><BitSize>3072</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Store</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: go to slot and deposit]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Retrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Command: go to slot and pick up]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nTargetSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Slot number (1–20)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sBatchIDToHandle</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which batch (for status messages)]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_AtTarget</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Position sensor: arrived at target]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>280</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_DepositDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Arm sensor: deposit complete]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_RetrieveDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Gripper: pick-up complete]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>296</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSim_Fault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive fault from VFD]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>304</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fSim_X_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ X encoder reading]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fSim_Y_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Y encoder reading]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_ASRSState</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stCurrentPos</Name><Type>ST_ASRSPosition</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>416</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stTargetPos</Name><Type>ST_ASRSPosition</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bReadyForCommand</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when crane is idle]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>736</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDepositComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: deposit finished]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>744</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrieveComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: retrieve finished]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>752</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHandoverComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: placed on output conveyor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>760</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>776</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonXTravel</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Timers]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1472</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonYTravel</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1728</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonDeposit</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>1984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonRetrieve</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>2240</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonHandover</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>2496</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFaultDelay</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>2752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Internal]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3008</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastStore</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3016</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrieveEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3024</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastRetrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3032</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bIsStoreOperation</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE=storing, FALSE=retrieving]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3040</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ASRSCoordinator</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_ASRSCoordinator
  ------------------
  The ASRS orchestrator — coordinates belt and crane together.
  PRG_MAIN only needs to call THIS ONE FB for all ASRS operations.
  Internally it creates and calls FB_ConveyorControl and FB_ASRSCrane.

  STORE sequence (state machine steps 0→5):
    0. Idle
    1. Place batch on input conveyor, start belt forward
    2. Wait for batch to reach ASRS entry sensor
    3. Command crane to move to target slot
    4. Wait for crane deposit confirmation
    5. Update database → signal bStorageComplete

  RETRIEVE sequence (steps 0, 10→15):
    0. Idle
   10. Command crane to target slot
   11. Wait for crane retrieve confirmation
   12. Crane returns to output conveyor
   13. Crane hands batch to output conveyor
   14. Start output conveyor reverse toward dispatch
   15. Wait for batch to reach dispatch → signal bRetrievalComplete
]]></Comment><BitSize>8576</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Store</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge: store this batch]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCmd_Retrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge: retrieve from this slot]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stBatchToStore</Name><Type>ST_MedicineBatch</Type><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nSlotToRetrieve</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which slot to retrieve from]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>992</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sRetrieveBatchID</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Batch ID being retrieved]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>1008</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dtNow</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1184</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStorageComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: batch physically in slot]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1216</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrievalComplete</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pulse: batch physically at dispatch]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBusy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1232</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eCoordState</Name><Type>E_ASRSState</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatusMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1264</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbInputConv</Name><Type>FB_ConveyorControl</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Sub-FB instances (internal)]]></Comment><BitSize>1472</BitSize><BitOffs>1920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbOutputConv</Name><Type>FB_ConveyorControl</Type><BitSize>1472</BitSize><BitOffs>3392</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbCrane</Name><Type>FB_ASRSCrane</Type><BitSize>3072</BitSize><BitOffs>4864</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nState</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ State machine]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>7936</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nWorkingSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Internal tracking]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>7952</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bStoreEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7968</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastStore</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7976</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRetrieveEdge</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bLastRetrieve</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7992</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonResetStorage</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Reset timers for pulse outputs]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>8000</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonResetRetrieval</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>8256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>8512</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_AlarmManager</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  FB_AlarmManager
  ---------------
  Centralized alarm handler using PRIORITY CHAIN logic.
  Higher alarm code number = lower priority.
  Emergency stop (100) ALWAYS beats temperature alarm (200), etc.

  Alarm Priority List (highest to lowest):
    100 — Emergency Stop      — stop everything immediately
    200 — Temperature alarm   — product quality at risk
    300 — Expired batch       — batch needs quarantine
    400 — Quarantine alarm    — batch has been isolated
    500 — ASRS fault          — mechanical problem
    600 — Rack full           — cannot accept new stock
    700 — Humidity alarm      — product quality at risk
]]></Comment><BitSize>832</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEmergencyStop</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExpiredFound</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bQuarantineAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bASRSFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bRackFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHumidityAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAnyAlarmActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>120</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nActiveAlarmCode</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sActiveAlarmMessage</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Method><Name>Execute</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_RackSlot</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_RackSlot
  -----------
  Represents one physical shelf slot in the Zone B storage rack.
  20 of these live in GVL_MedicineDB.astRackSlots[1..20].
  Layout: 4 columns × 5 rows.
  Slot numbering: Slot 1-4 = Row 1, Slot 5-8 = Row 2, etc.
]]></Comment><BitSize>320</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nSlotID</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Slot number 1 to 20]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nColumn</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Physical column 1 to 4]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nRow</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Physical row 1 to 5]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bOccupied</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = batch is sitting here]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sBatchID</Name><Type>STRING(20)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Which batch is here (empty if free)]]></Comment><BitSize>168</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fCurrentWeight_kg</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Simulated load cell reading]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fPhysicalX_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ X position in warehouse (mm)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fPhysicalY_mm</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Y position in warehouse (mm)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_EnvironmentData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_EnvironmentData
  ------------------
  A complete snapshot of Zone C environmental conditions.
  FB_EnvironmentControl reads sensor inputs and writes all fields here.
  One instance lives in GVL_MedicineDB.stEnvData.
]]></Comment><BitSize>576</BitSize><SubItem><Name>fTemperature_C</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current temperature in °C]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fHumidity_Pct</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current relative humidity in %]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fTempSetpoint_C</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Target temperature (default 15.0°C)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fHumidSetpoint_Pct</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Target humidity (default 40.0%)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCoolingActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = cooling system is running]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHeatingActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = heating system is running]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = temperature outside safe range]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bHumidityAlarm</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = humidity outside safe range]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>sStatus</Name><Type>STRING(50)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ e.g. 'ENVIRONMENT OK' or 'COOLING ACTIVE']]></Comment><BitSize>408</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>E_SystemMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  E_SystemMode
  ------------
  The master operating mode of the entire warehouse system.
  Think of this as the system's current "gear".
  PRG_MAIN sets this every scan cycle based on what is happening.
  The HMI displays this as the main status indicator.
]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_IDLE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ System waiting, no active operation]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_RECEIVING</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Zone A is processing a new batch]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_STORING</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ASRS is placing a batch in a rack slot]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_RETRIEVING</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ASRS is pulling a batch for dispatch]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_QUARANTINE</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Quarantine operation in progress]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_EMERGENCY</Text><Enum>5</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ E-Stop active — all motion halted]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_MAINTENANCE</Text><Enum>6</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Manual override — technician working]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_SystemAlarms</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
  ST_SystemAlarms
  ---------------
  All alarm flags and codes for the entire system.
  Think of this as the dashboard warning lights on a car.
  One instance lives in GVL_SystemState.stAlarms.
